ingle B8, since B8 can only form chow B678/B789 (B6 is gone? B6: out count = 1? unseen 0? Actually check unseen B6: start 4, across player meld B678 (B6, B7, B8) uses one B6, your B456 uses one B6, one discarded earlier, so maybe 1 left? possible but unlikely).  \n\nB8's chow needs B6B7B8 or B7B8B9, both hard. So B8 weak.  \n\n**Danger tiles:** F3\u00d73 left in hand, opponents may need F3 for pung? No F3 discarded yet. Actually game history shows previous player played F4, not F3. Unseen F3 count: start 4, you have 3, none discarded, so only 1 left in wall. Safe for others to pung? Someone could have a pair waiting. But F3 discard from you is risky if someone has pair. So safer to keep F3 as meld and not discard F3.  \n\nSo viable discards: T1, B8, F4, T7.  \nB8 is safer than T1 (terminal) maybe.  \n\nAlso consider scoring: with F1 pung (Prevalent+Seat wind 2 fan) + maybe All Types (W+ B + T + Wind + Dragon). You have B, T, Wind(F1,F3,F4), no Dragon yet, so missing Dragon for All Types.  \n\nBut quickest tenpai may be if you draw another T7 \u2192 T7 pung, then need meld from T1+B8+F4 impossible. So not ready.  \n\nGiven the hand is far from ready, safe discard is key. Unshown tiles count suggests B8 and T1 are relatively safe. T1: unseen W1 0, so not relevant. T1: start 4 T1, game history shows T1 discarded by you and by others, so maybe 1 left unseen. B8: start 4, meld by across player (B678) used 1, maybe discards used some, unseen possibly 1 left too.  \n\nChoose B8 to keep wind tiles for possible fan (since you have F1, F3, F4, might get wind pung related points).  \n\n**Evaluation:** Discard B8 is safest, keeps wind pung, T7\u00d72 for potential pair/chow, T1 for terminal pair chance.  \n\n**Reason:** B8 is isolated, chow chances low, safer discard. F3 triple kept as concealed pung for potential fan. Hand remains flexible to draw into T6/T8/T9 or another T7 to form meld.  \n\n**Answer:** Play B8"}
